# S-PUBLISH 09. A build that was never stamped INVENTS a commit for itself -- forty zeros,
# defect: which is a real-looking SHA -- instead of reporting that it does not know.
#
# WHY THIS SHAPE. "Unknown" degrading into a plausible answer is this file's own recorded
# incident, one costume along: the old drift watcher fell back to an mtime compare whenever the
# stamp was missing, and looped 64 times in an afternoon. `publish --exe <prebuilt>` reaches the
# unstamped case on EVERY call, so a substitute value here is not a corner.
#
# THE PAIRED RED (plan 5.3). The acceptance ancestor read it back out of `version --json`:
#
#   prebuilt_publish_claims_no_provenance: FAIL commit=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
#
# expects-red: unit:Dodona.Tests.PublishPlanTests.prebuilt_publish_claims_no_provenance
#
# The control. Target resolution has nothing to do with provenance, and a mutant that reddened
# both would be measuring the suite rather than the seam.
#
# expects-green: unit:Dodona.Tests.PublishPlanTests.all_reaches_every_live_workspace
diff --git a/src/Dodona/Ver.cs b/src/Dodona/Ver.cs
index 1e96757..e3eb278 100644
